{title: 20 Cigarettes}
{artist: Morgan Wallen}
{key: A}
{tempo: 98}
{comment: Standard tuning, key A — no capo.}

{start_of_intro: pickup}
|F#m| |D| |A| |E|
Vocal and guitar only — "We burned..." enters on B section feel, then D on "13 cigarettes".
{end_of_intro}

{start_of_verse}
Twenty [F#m]cigarettes and I [D]lit me one
On that [A]redwood deck on De-[E]monbreun
She was [F#m]with her friends, left 'em [D]standin' there
There was [A]more than smoke in that [E]summer air
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
We burnt [D]two while she told me bout' her hometown
She was drinkin' [F#m]Titos, said I better slow down
I was like, [A]hell no, I ain't drinkin' by my-[E]self, no
Said she loved my [D]accent so I kept talkin'
Reached for the [F#m]pack on the table by my wallet
We tore [A]off to light the [E]night we had [D]left
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
With thirteen [F#m]cigarettes and I [D]lit me one
With the [A]windows cracked in my [E]old half-ton
Singin' [F#m]take me home on them [D]country roads
So I turned [A]off on one then next [E]thing you know
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
We had a beer [D]bottle lookin' like an ashtray
Under that [F#m]full moon she was 'bout halfway
Naked in my [A]truck bed, so I helped her with the [F#m]rest
She was sayin' [D]my name, barely even knew it
We were both [F#m]lyin', said we [E]never do this
To the [E]music of the wind through the [D]woods
{end_of_chorus}

